{"_id":"codex:protocol:06:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"protocol","title":"Protocol of Strategy Orchestration","seq":306,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","protocol","strategy"],"notes":"Coordinates actions→strategies→goals→dreams using resonance vectors and policy budgets."}
{"_id":"codex:protocol:06:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"policy","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"protocol","title":"Protocol of Strategy Orchestration","seq":306,"version":"1.0.0","body":"1) Group actions into strategies; strategies into goals; goals into dreams. 2) Compute resonance vectors and their opposites for each node; admit nodes with ethical thresholds satisfied. 3) Build execution trees optimized for efficiency under energy/attention/risk/trust budgets. 4) Route irreversible nodes by TII to quorum/tribunal. 5) Emit signed intents and lineage before actuation."}
{"_id":"codex:protocol:06:refs","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"index","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"protocol","title":"Protocol of Strategy Orchestration References","seq":306,"version":"1.0.0","refs":["codex:chapter:02","codex:chapter:09","codex:scroll:04"],"notes":"References reflection, tribunal, and transparency."}